# Why: A-01 in the 2026-09-10 security audit — an anonymous authorization
#      bypass. Documenso's admin authorization lives ONLY in the admin layout
#      loader (`admin+/_layout.tsx`). Under React Router 7 single-fetch, a
#      request for `/admin/<page>.data?_routes=routes/_authenticated+/admin+/<page>`
#      runs that leaf loader alone and skips every ancestor loader, so the
#      layout check never runs and each unguarded admin leaf loader returns
#      tenant data (documents with recipients/fields/signatures/signing tokens,
#      user emails, organisation insights, the CAPTCHA secret) to anyone. Eight
#      upstream admin leaf loaders were unguarded; each now calls
#      `requireAdminLoader(request)` (packages/bizrethink/server-only/
#      require-admin-loader.ts), the same isAdmin gate the fork's own admin
#      pages already use, returning 404 to anonymous and non-admin callers.
#
# Why not a new file: these are upstream Documenso route files; the guard has
#      to run inside each of their loaders. The gate logic itself is a new
#      owned file in packages/bizrethink; this patch only wires it in.
#
# Fragility: MEDIUM. Upstream owns these route files and single-fetch route
#      filtering is framework behaviour. A future sync that adds a new admin
#      page, or reformats these, conflicts here — but the failure is loud:
#      packages/bizrethink/regression-tests/admin-loaders-gated.test.ts scans
#      the admin route dir and fails on any leaf loader that gates neither via
#      requireAdminLoader nor isAdmin, and require-admin-loader.test.ts pins the
#      helper's 404-for-anon/non-admin behaviour.
